{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Noah began, a man of the soil, and planted a vineyard.</b> The reason Scripture juxtaposed the matter of wine to the sign of the rainbow may be explained as follows: because wine alludes to the attribute of strict judgment (midat ha-din), as you know; and on this the Sages, of blessed memory, said that one does not recite a blessing over wine until he puts water into it." "<b>And know</b> that there was no man who contemplated this matter until Noah came, for the early ones each planted a vine for himself individually, but Noah now began to plant vines in rows, which is called a כרם (vineyard); and this is the sense of ויחל ('he began')." "<b>Alternatively,</b> it may be explained that since Noah was the tenth generation and 'the tenth is holy,' when he now engaged in the matter of wine it became חולין (profane) — and this is the sense of ויחל. And Scripture tells us of many great and grave troubles for which wine was the cause: for it caused the righteous, blameless man who had saved the entire world to sin, and brought it about that his descendant be cursed. Behold, this passage is a warning against wine like the passage of the nazirite, or even more so; and likewise the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded in Sanhedrin (70a): thirteen וי״ן (vavs) are said concerning wine — ויחל, וישת, וישכר, ויתגל, וירא חם, ויגד, ויקח, שם ויפת, וישימו וילכו אחורנית ויכסו, ויקץ, וידע. And so Solomon said (Proverbs 23:29): ״למי אוי למי אבוי למי מדינים למי שיח וגו״. And the intent is not concerning wine alone, for the same applies to all other worldly lusts: whoever is drawn after them is banished from this world and from the world to come; and wine is the father of them all, for it is what causes the destruction of body and soul. And Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Ecclesiastes 2:25): ״כי מי יאכל ומי יחוש חוץ ממני״ — that is, who stood upon the pleasures of the world, and who enjoyed the bodily senses more than I? And after it he said: ״גם זה הבל״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:31.327425454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}